.TH scan_to_sa 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/textcode"
.SH NAME
scan_to_sa \- Scan data and store it into a stralloc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/textcode.h>
.sp
.BI "size_t scan_to_sa(size_t (*func)(const char*, char*, size_t*), const char* src, stralloc* sa)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR scan_to_sa () scans data and stores it into a stralloc. The function takes the following parameters:
.sp
1. A pointer to a scanning function that takes a source string, a destination buffer, and a pointer to the size of the destination buffer, and returns the number of bytes processed from the source string.
2. A pointer to the source string.
3. A pointer to the destination stralloc.
.sp
The function returns the number of bytes processed from the source string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes processed from the source string.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B stralloc, str
